WEBVTT

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.580
Carlos Rivera...

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:26.040
He's one hell of a guy.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.370
I wonder what their announcement is gonna be.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.960
Beats me, I haven't got a clue.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:08.620
The way I see it...

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:15.420
they're probably going to rationalize Carlos Rivera's past couple of fights, which, although he won,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.060
were contrary to his title as a world-ranked boxer.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.180
Am I right?

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:19.880
Yeah, that makes sense...

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.020
Well, that may actually be a good move.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:27.480
They phone up a bunch of newspaper reporters and get them here,

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:30.860
only to say "We apologize for all the trouble we caused you."

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.400
That happens more often than you'd think!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.940
The shocking confession, you mean?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.940
Yeah, exactly!

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.730
But it's a bit of a disappointment, I guess.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.910
I thank you all for taking time out of your busy schedule to come here.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:54.210
Yesterday, the Commissioner gave the official go-ahead

00:03:54.210 --> 00:04:00.460
for a match between the All-Japan Bantamweight Champion Tiger Ozaki and Carlos Rivera.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.430
Oh? Carlos is fighting Tiger Ozaki?

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:09.890
Naturally, this match will be a no-title ten-round match,

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.990
but before this match, Carlos' manager, Robert,

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.820
has an announcement to make regarding this match.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.820
Excuse me.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.820
He says he's got an announcement to make...

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:21.820
<i>What could it be?</i>

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.410
Sure, he's gotten the go-ahead from the Commissioner,

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.700
but maybe he's gonna withdraw due to Carlos' poor condition?

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.910
Yeah, that's gotta be it!

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.660
He'll do it before the "world-ranked boxer" is exposed for the fraud he is!

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:34.990
<i>I have a prediction to make.</i>

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.000
Oh, I get it.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:34.990
Maybe he'll say

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:38.550
he's returning to his homeland for urgent business,

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:39.550
<i>Carlos will win by KO in the first round.</i>

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.670
or something along those lines...

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.890
I feel very bad for Tiger Ozaki,

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.930
but this is a pure and simple fact.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.400
Pardon me, I couldn't quite make that out. Could you say it again?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:03.400
Listen. Carlos Rivera will knock out Tiger Ozaki in round one!

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.490
Knock him out in round one?

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.420
<i>¡No!</i>

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.120
Not just one round...

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.120
<i>¡Un minuto!</i>

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:18.630
One minute.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:22.050
Within one minute,

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.890
Tiger Ozaki...

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.270
will be knocked out.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.230
Within one minute?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:53.710
Excellent, Carlos.

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.300
That is an excellent challenge to Yabuki Joe.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.560
You've really done it now, Carlos.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:17.430
"This unprecedented declaration that he will KO

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:21.690
the All-Japan Champion Tiger Ozaki in the first minute of the first round

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:25.780
may be a publicity stunt to restore some of Carlos' dropping popularity,

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.620
but it is nothing more than a farce."

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:28.700
What the hell?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:31.410
A farce, my ass!

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:32.830
They don't know a damn thing!

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.080
You think so too, old man?

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:41.880
Either way, Carlos is starting to show his true colors.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.840
The black panther is finally baring his fangs,

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.680
after acting like a tame house cat for so long.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.130
Sure, his opponent may be a tiger,

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:55.650
but once he faces the All-Japan Champion, 
he'll become a panther and go straight for the jugular.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.020
That's pretty clever.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.650
And on top of that, he added in a KO prediction.

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:06.020
Now, after the panther's killed the tiger, what's his next prey?

00:07:06.020 --> 00:07:07.570
You know, don't you, old man?

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.840
What, you don't?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.420
The black panther's next prey is gonna be me!

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:23.500
The great Yabuki Joe!

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:27.460
It's gonna happen, old man! Carlos and I are gonna fight!

00:07:27.970 --> 00:07:30.510
Wow, that was pretentious even by my standards!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.440
The black panther and the scarred wolf...

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:25.770
Hey, it's pretty empty.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.620
Isn't this a sorry sight?

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:34.910
I know the main event hasn't started yet,

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.580
but talk about a slow night.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:56.560
She seems to be in a good mood, considering the lack of an audience.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.810
She looks as excited as if she were hosting a party.

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.310
Pardon me, I assume you're the chairman of Tange Gym and Yabuki-san?

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:07.770
I hate to bother, but Shiraki-san asked me to show you to your special ringside seats.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:09.240
Special seats?

00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.950
Yes. Shiraki-san had them reserved for you both.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.440
She wanted you to have a better view.

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.450
Tell her to mind her own business.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.490
But...

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:19.540
Forget it!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:21.410
If I can't see well, I'll just move to an empty seat.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.420
Go tell that to Shiraki-san!

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:27.090
Y-Yes, sir.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:27.980
Joe!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.100
She's still got that high-and-mighty look of hers.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.220
I guess she hasn't changed, either!

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.560
<i>The judges have decided that the winner of this match is Obata!</i>

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.040
All right! The main event's finally up next!

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:46.980
About time!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.480
Alley-oop! Hup! Hop!

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:54.740
Here we go.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.030
Hey, old man! There's an open seat over here!

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.410
Come on and get down here!

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:01.290
All right, all right! Just don't shout!

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.290
Good to see you well, my lady!

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.500
I see you're doing just fine, as well.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.960
Yeah, thank god.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.500
So with the stands this empty,

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:13.300
won't this put Shiraki Yohko, the promoter,

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:17.510
pretty far in the red, considering the fee you paid to bring Carlos over?

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.140
But you're an heiress to a powerful magnate.

00:10:20.140 --> 00:10:22.510
I guess a little bit of a loss is nothing to you.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.940
Hey, Joe! Leave her alone!

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:29.480
Hey, hey, hey! Go for it, Tiger!

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.280
This is your shot at the world rankings!

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.020
We're counting on it!

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:35.480
Yeah, yeah, Carlos!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.030
You better roll over and give up today!

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:42.490
That's what we came here to see!

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:45.490
Hey, your joke about the one-minute KO was really funny!

00:10:45.490 --> 00:10:48.580
Yeah, it was really cute!

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:52.050
Hey, Carlos! Tiger's the champion, you know!

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.050
You understand me?

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:57.500
If you think you can get lucky like you did with Nango and Harajima, you're dead wrong!

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:00.220
Hey, lookie at that!

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.680
Carlos looks awful meek today!

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.970
Well, of course he is! He told a big whopper he can't live up to!

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.770
Guess he knows tonight is the end.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:08.980
Oh, that must be it!

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:12.980
One minute, my ass, you goddamn fraud!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:15.410
Don't think you can mess with the Tiger!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.550
Joe, did you hear my one-minute prediction?

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:36.170
Oh, I sure did!

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.760
Now I'm gonna see what you got!

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.720
Carlos...

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:48.190
You predicted you'd knock him out in one minute...

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:50.680
and I'm gonna see that with my own eyes!

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:55.690
Joe... Knowing you're watching will make this all the more worth it.

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:10.410
The match is finally starting!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.840
What will Tiger's camp do?

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.920
We'd like to see him, the All-Japan Champion, crush the one-minute KO declaration,

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.930
erase that insult, and make his way into the world rankings.

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:23.850
In the other corner, how will Carlos Rivera uphold his honor as the sixth-ranked fighter in the world,

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:27.230
and make the one-minute KO prediction come true?

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:02.590
Son of a...

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:08.740
Here I go!

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.910
S-Sixteen seconds?

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:36.890
Doctor! Doctor, hurry!

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.390
Oh... Right.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.900
What a surprise...

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:43.780
Tiger...

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:45.910
Tiger!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:06.340
Very, very nice, Carlos.

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.430
<i>Gracias,</i> Robert.

00:15:09.180 --> 00:15:11.340
<i>Gracias,</i> Senorita Yohko.

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:29.860
Mr. Carlos Rivera!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.130
Well, that was a surprise!

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.830
He actually did it in just sixteen seconds!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.380
In just sixteen seconds since the bell rang in the match,

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.830
he made true on his prediction!

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:52.840
Carlos' win by KO made all our hairs stand on end!

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:56.640
Who could have possibly guessed this would happen?

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.970
Yeah, not bad!

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:02.560
Way to go, Venezuelan Champ!

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.360
You go, man!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:11.780
Hey, Joe!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.820
Well, that's a world-ranked boxer for you!

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:16.830
Well done, well done!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.490
Excellent, excellent!

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.170
Nicely done!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.290
Nicely done!

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:27.510
Very nice!

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:30.720
The one-round KO prediction we had all taken as a joke

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.840
was dramatically made true by Carlos Rivera with a hard right,

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:38.270
which can only be described as terrifying!

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:41.230
We've now brought Carlos over into the broadcasting booth.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:45.070
That really was an impressive punch back there, Mr. Carlos!

00:16:45.070 --> 00:16:47.690
Pardon me for the rude question,

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:51.410
but we were quite shocked at this compared to your first and second matches,

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.530
so was this punch lucky like the others?

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:54.620
Lucky?

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:57.660
Robert, how should I answer him?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.780
Good question, I'm not so sure...

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:05.290
This was all planned out by Miss Yohko, the promoter that brought us to Japan...

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.760
The curtain's fallen now.

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:10.300
You can tell him anything you want, Robert.

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:11.970
Yes, but Miss Yohko,

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:15.300
this is all too hard for me to say.

00:17:23.190 --> 00:17:25.010
Then allow me to be frank.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:29.400
Tonight's one-punch KO was the result of pure, unquestionable skill,

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.360
and he can pull off this stunt whenever he so desires.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:37.820
Y-You mean his poor fighting in the Nango and Harajima fights was all just an act?

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.960
We have traveled all around the world,

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.830
and have done the same thing in every country we've gone to.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:46.340
Every country?

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:50.710
That's right. Otherwise, nobody would let him fight!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:54.300
If every country knew his skill, his competitors would all run and hide!

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:57.430
I see now. So that was an act.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:00.600
Still, you deserve an Academy Award for being able to pull off an act like that!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.360
Very impressive, Mr. Carlos!

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:10.730
I am not an actor.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.370
I have no desire for an Oscar.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.820
Don't get so mad, Carlos.

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:20.160
This is very tragic for you as a boxer,

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:21.530
but we have no choice.

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.710
I know, Robert.

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.710
I'm sorry.

00:18:26.380 --> 00:18:29.500
But just once is enough...

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:33.850
I want to fight in this bright, shining ring...

00:18:34.510 --> 00:18:36.510
This ring that smells of turpentine...

00:18:37.430 --> 00:18:38.930
and have a match

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:42.930
where I can set my very life aflame, not as an actor, but as a true boxer!

00:18:51.280 --> 00:18:53.570
That is my dream.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:57.570
And I have become an actor to fulfill that dream.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:02.490
I'm impressed.

00:19:02.490 --> 00:19:03.950
I'm real impressed!

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.580
I'm impressed, Carlos!

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.080
You sure know how to talk like a pro!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.470
I'm getting chills!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.080
Nice one!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.040
Just look at him. Yabuki's shouting again.

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:20.470
Poor guy. He must be letting out his disappointment knowing he couldn't stand a chance against him.

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:19.240
<i>Hell yeah! Hell yeah! Rah-rah, Carlos!</i>

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:21.680
Well, what can I say?

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:21.920
<i>That's right, baby!</i>

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:26.600
Yabuki Joe once raised some hell in the ring, so much he was known as Joe the Wild,

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:22.680
<i>Let go!</i>

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:29.940
so his frolicking now just seems pitiful.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.690
By the way, Mr. Carlos,

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:34.060
now that you have defeated the All-Japan Champion, Tiger,

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.830
I assume that means you have no more business in Japan...

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:38.780
So which country do you plan on fighting in next?

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:40.110
<i>He's not going anywhere.</i>

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:43.110
He plans on staying in Japan for a while.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:47.410
Oh, I see. Then I hope you enjoy your restful visit in Japan, and enjoy the sights...

00:19:47.410 --> 00:19:48.500
<i>No gracias.</i>

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.710
I have no interest in sightseeing.

00:19:50.710 --> 00:19:52.170
Only boxing.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.850
That is why I have come all the way to Japan.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:58.720
W-Well, I suppose so, but you don't have any more opponents here...

00:19:58.720 --> 00:19:59.810
Oh, I do!

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:05.140
But you've dominated the entire All-Japan Bantamweight Division,

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.430
with Nango, Harajima, and now the Champion, Tiger...

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:10.100
There is one more champion.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:12.100
Wh-Where?

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:13.650
Over there.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.610
He is right there!

00:20:16.650 --> 00:20:20.330
He may not be a champion, but Joe Yabuki is the uncrowned emperor!

00:20:20.330 --> 00:20:26.700
And this uncrowned emperor is far stronger than the one that holds the champion's belt!

00:20:29.670 --> 00:20:30.750
My dream...

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:34.750
The opponent I can set my life aflame against is Joe Yabuki!

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:37.800
I played my act in the Nango and Harajima matches

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.710
as a challenge to Joe!

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.720
My KO prediction was for that sake as well!

00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:45.350
And the fact that I have defeated Tiger as I predicted

00:20:45.350 --> 00:20:47.720
means that I have issued my final challenge

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:51.220
to Joe Yabuki, my dream!

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:55.730
Joe, will you accept my challenge?

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:58.730
Yeah! I accept!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.630
Now this is a very unusual challenge!

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:23.550
Normally, challenges are formally issued through the Commissioner-

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:27.590
Formal or not, I will fight wherever and whenever necessary!

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.640
Yeah! I feel the same way, Señor Carlos!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:17.770
Joe...

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:22.280
Whoa, hold it. Don't say a thing, old man.

00:22:22.280 --> 00:22:24.690
The die has already been cast.

00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.700
The die has been cast...

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:15.870
The wind's starting to get cold...

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:18.040
It sure feels like autumn...

00:24:42.120 --> 00:24:45.340
Joe's match with Carlos is faced with its greatest crisis!

00:24:45.340 --> 00:24:49.250
Carlos is finally faced with a chance for the world title!

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:52.760
Carlos, desiring to face Joe, harshly opposes Robert!

00:24:53.800 --> 00:24:56.640
And Joe shows up before the troubled Carlos,

00:24:56.640 --> 00:25:00.770
to give him a helping hand to make his final decision!

00:25:00.770 --> 00:25:02.740
Now, the match draws near,

00:25:02.740 --> 00:25:06.070
and as Joe and Carlos fiercely set their lives ablaze,

00:25:06.070 --> 00:25:07.900
which way is tomorrow!?
